    "insights": [
      "LU decomposition (O(n^3/3)) and Gaussian elimination have the same leading complexity - luMuls = gaussMuls",
      "QR factorization (O(4n^3/3)) is at most 2x Gaussian - qrMuls = 2*gaussMuls",
      "QR beats Cramer only for n >= 3: at n=1, tie (both 2); at n=2, QR=16 > Cramer=12",
      "Key lemma: 2n^3 < n^2*n! for n>=4 via 2n^3 < n^4 = n^2*n^2 < n^2*n!",
      "All O(n^3) algorithms asymptotically beat Cramer by any constant factor K"
